{"uid":"modules/loop/triage_scheduler.py","name":"triage_scheduler.py","qualname":"modules/loop/triage_scheduler.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/loop/triage_scheduler.py","line":1,"end_line":179,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Difficulty-triage scheduling for the autonomous multi-target loop.","description":"Ports the sapper-v2 scheduling doctrine into LazyOwn terms: a short triage\nestimates each target's difficulty, the queue is drained easy-first so quick\nwins land before hard assaults, a stop-loss abandons targets that burn attempts\nwithout progress, and near a deadline partially-solved targets are salvaged\nfirst. The scheduler is pure: it operates on plain task records (dicts) and\nperforms no I/O, so the engine can order its own queue and the policy stays\nunit-testable in isolation.\n\nTask records may carry these optional triage fields; all default to neutral so\nan unannotated queue degrades to easy-first-by-arrival ordering:\n    ``difficulty`` (0.0 easy .. 1.0 hard), ``attempts`` (int),\n    ``progress`` (0.0 .. 1.0), ``partial`` (bool, has salvageable partial).","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/loop/triage_scheduler.py::estimate_difficulty","modules/loop/triage_scheduler.py::TriageScheduler"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
